            "review_title": "Review at Valhalla Grill",
            "review_text": "Vandergast\nMorelia, Mexico198 contributions\n0\nThe food is good; not the setting.\nMay 2019 • Couples\nThis restaurant has the bad luck to be located next to the most popular burger place in Da Nang. So, comparing both restaurants will be a common thing. \n\nGood points: \n1. Some items from the menu are really good like the cheese fingers and chili poppers. The hot dogs and pull-pork burger are good. \n2. The staff is extremely welcoming and helpful. \n\nPoints to improve: \n1. The setting is really bad. It has no character at all. The seating is uncomfortable. \n2. The falafel burger is very dry. It needs more sauces, veggies, or something to moist the burger. \nThe kitchen area is in front; so it becomes very hot in there. The fans just don’t do much to cool the place. \n3. The washroom is in the back with all the food storage. \n\nOverall, the food is not bad. Give it a try if the place next door is full. But they’ll have to compete to bring the restaurant to the next level. Have better drink selection and take note of what other successful restaurants are doing.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nWritten May 4, 2019",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-04",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
            "feature_depth_status": "Schema-Full-Features-Validated"
