            "reviewer_id": "User_p1_13",
            "review_title": "Review at Valhalla Grill",
            "review_text": "roger s\nLondon, United Kingdom57 contributions\n0\nDo not eat here\nJan 2019 • Friends\nHad burgers, menu looks good but saw big foam boxes on the floor in the kitchen with thawed up vacuum packed meats that had clearly been delivered frozen, I expect the meat would be either put in a fridge or re-frozen since there was a lot of meat, very unsanitary, my friend was sick for two days after our meal here. No way to recommend this place.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten January 12, 2019\nJeppe H\nHi Roger - I am happy that you noticed the isolated styrofoam boxes in Valhalla Grill, this is the sanitary way that we transport the food items from our central kitchen in Hanoi to Da Nang. The boxes are thick foam walled boxes to make sure the food is transported safely and does not defrost on the way on the cooling truck. \n\nYou write that you had the burgers and your friend got sick for 2 days after eating in our place, please consider the fact that your friend could have gotten sick from many other sources in your trip - 1. It is almost impossible to get sick from beef 2. we serve over 1000 people daily in our 5 shops, and as you can see from our reviews, this is not a problem we have.\n\nI am sorry your friend got sick, but i am very confident it was not from our food.\n\nGlad you visited us and i sincerely hope you will contact me/us if you have any questions about our food safety and production - We put great care into this.\nRead more\nWritten January 13, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
