            "review_title": "Review at Valhalla Grill",
            "review_text": "Rhubarb & Custard\nDa Nang, Vietnam35 contributions\n0\nCheap and cheerful\nDec 2018 • Friends\nLow quality, frozen beef patties with very little flavour. French fries also frozen. It's very cheap and okay for a fast food craving, but there are much better burgers in town for similar prices.\nWritten December 8, 2018\nJeppe H\nAll our food items are made in our central kitchen in Hanoi. 48 hour slow cooked pulled pork, imported Australian and South American beef that we mince, season and prepare for cooking in our shops. Our chicken in sous vide cooked at 61c to maintain moisture and texture. All our sauces are made fresh and are hand made by us. Just because it is cheap doesn't mean it is not good. We spend months for each product before it is launched, testing researching and tasting - Also getting feedback from our customers. I am sorry if you find our food tasteless, we can not satisfy everyone. But we try our best.\nRead more\nWritten January 13, 2019\nThis response is the subjective opinion of the management representative and not of Tripadvisor LLC nor of its partners.",
